  <entry>
    <title>Introduction to Sampling and Generative Algorithms</title>
    <link href="https://rpche-6626.github.io/2026/02/24/SP/IntroToSampling/"/>
    <id>https://rpche-6626.github.io/2026/02/24/SP/IntroToSampling/</id>
    <published>2026-02-23T16:00:00.000Z</published>
    <updated>2026-02-24T13:42:31.000Z</updated>
    
    
    <summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;You know that I was writing these notes in Chinese for convenience
and better expression. However later I realized that these things are
written mostly for peers, so I am writing in English from now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have discussed a few aspects of deep generative models in previous
parts, specifically VAE and a brief cover (from MIT 6.S184) of diffusion
and flow models. As I finished CS3936 I realized that these theories are
merely an aspect of stochastic interpolants. So I decide to have a more
detailed discussion on these closely related sampling and generative
algorithms along with basic mathematical tools and more detailed proofs,
as I intend to pursue such fields in the future.&lt;/p&gt;</summary>
    
    
    
